cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Beloch in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Beloch: a declarative language for origami"
abstract: >-
  Beloch evaluates a declarative source program, written as a sequence of
  Huzita-Justin axiom operations, into a folded state and a crease pattern.
  The evaluator works over an exact real-algebraic number kernel, so
  constructed coincidences hold exactly rather than within a tolerance, and
  emits the FOLD interchange format.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mühl"
    given-names: "Christopher"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4692-078X"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-09-22"
license: MIT
